# curated/

The decisions made about the data, by hand or by a model, that the sources can't give back: they cost time (yours)
or money (a model's) to make. The database holds them. These files are their copy in git.

- **Written after the database, by the commands.** A command that changes a decision (`label`, `unlabel`, or
  `/fix-curation`) changes the database, then rewrites these files from it. Don't edit them by hand: the next
  command overwrites your edit.
- **Read only to rebuild a database.** After the database is lost or rebuilt (`/rebuild-database`), `ingest` loads
  them back. Until then, every other command that changes a decision refuses to run. In normal work, nothing reads
  them.
- **Guarded by git.** The pre-commit hook (`curated-check`) shows what each commit does to these files. It stops a
  commit that empties one or loses many rows, until you confirm with `ALLOW_CURATED_LOSS=1`.
  `git checkout HEAD -- curated/` brings them back.
- **Sorted**, so `git diff` shows exactly which decisions changed.
- **Private.** They are your decisions: this repo stays private. `doctor --remote` fails if it is public.

`classified_by` is `manual` (you) or `llm` (a model). A model never overwrites a manual decision.

## labels.csv: one row per labelled day

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `day` | the day |
| `label` | what was special about it (a holiday, a broken meter) |
| `classified_by`, `classified_at` | who decided it, and when |
| `note` | why, for later |
